how do I find an internship if you are  young if you're just starting out if you  want to learn about an industry one of  the best ways to do it is to become an  intern at a company that you respect  that you look up to that you want to  emulate and figure out is this path for  you or not I always encourage young  people to try as many things as possible  so you don't get locked into one thing  too early you have to find what your  life's passion is what your purpose is  and that comes from exploring a lot of  different options and not get too down  on yourself when you haven't found it  because a lot of people get locked into  something way too early and then they're  stuck the rest of their lives doing this  one thing and they end up hating it more  and more and more and wishing they had  some other option when you're young you  have the ability to try all these things  out before you have you know burdens  before you have responsibilities before  you have to you know a spouse kids house  mortgage all those things to worry about  now is your time go out explore learn  what you are meant to do and if it  doesn't work out at some position three  months six months leaving go to  something else it's okay to bounce  around now how do you get that  internship it's a question I got from  one of my YouTube viewers Berta  thank you guys I love getting the  questions on YouTube Berta wrote to say  I'm a marketing student I'm trying to  find an internship and marketing  consultancy  I love branding and basically it goes on  but basically has not been able to find  an internship for one of the companies  she's looked at and one of my advice on  how to go and get this internship so  here's what I would do if I was trying  to get an internship I would first look  at the ideal companies that I want to  work for and where are you going to get  the most learning opportunity okay if  you're doing it just for a resume then  the bigger companies look better but if  you're doing it to really learn you're  going to get much more hands-on  experience working for a smaller company  because the big companies don't really  value their interns too much you're  going to be doing pretty boring jobs  you'll be learning a little bit and  you'll get the name on the resume but  you're not going to really increase your  skills and in my opinion if you're going  to take a job if you're going to go work  for somebody else  you want to do something where you're  going to learn something you're not  doing it for the money you're not doing  it for the resume you're doing it to  learn and so the best opportunities will  come with the smaller companies and the  smaller companies may not even have an  internship program here's the thing I  look at look for any entrepreneur look  for a company that you respect maybe ten  employees around that size so they're  not just starting up but they're doing  some amazing work and they're small  enough that if you join them you'll have  a ton of work to do every entrepreneur  has tons of work that they would love to  give to somebody tons they are  struggling they are they are in way over  their heads they are working crazy  number of hours they need reliable  people that they can count on and if  you're looking for even you said a free  internship that's something that people  would scoop up so I try to find an  entrepreneur that you look up to is  doing some amazing work that you one day  might want to emulate have your own  marketing consultancy company and making  that you know ten people plus type of  business find them out and contact them  let them know what you're doing just  like this passion email you sent me here  on YouTube because they may not even  thought of an internship program but  they are always looking for people who  are talented passionate and want to  learn and once you get in once you go  meet them let them know why you want to  do this what you hope to accomplish  because not enough employees are  passionate enough about the work that  they're doing if you come in with  passion excitement for marketing for  branding you're going to blow them away  especially if it's free to start they're  going to be crazy for not hiring you  that's your first step once you get in  you want to learn as much as you can  about the business you want to be  mentored by the entrepreneur you want to  take on as many projects as you can and  you're going to figure out if this  business is for you or not and don't  don't accept just a project they give  you ask for more no employee asks for  more right nobody asks to do more than  what they're given this is your chance  to stand out to shine to really learn  the business and if you're doing a great  job they're going to be fools not to  hire you not to want to turn this into a  full-time position for you and that's  going to be a pretty fortunate position  for you to be in and you'll discover is  this the business that you want to learn  from or not if it is you continue on if  it's not  go in turn somewhere else different  business if an industry and that's okay  until you figure out what you're born to  do so I would continue on my path if you  really need that resume just the name  keep going after the big companies who  have formal programs that's okay but I  think you're going to get a lot better  education and a lot better personal  development working for a smaller  company who doesn't even have an  internship program and you can be the  first person to join them this is one  quick aside I never had a huge  internship program I don't even think of  the concept and a school came to me and  said we'd like to do an internship  program with you  I thought that's a really cool idea and  one of the first people that came in was  a guy named Addis who was from Holland  and he came to Canada where I am and  needed a job opportunity so it was it  was a free internship and he became one  of my programmers to help out and  designing my website programming  designing the website and he was great  and he hustled and he worked and and I  felt the passion when I first met him  and it continued and I hired him and  he's still with me now and this is maybe  six seven years later he's still on the  team he's still developing new stuff for  the website and so if you show your  passion and your excitement to an  entrepreneur who has that same passion  excited who wants to build something  special you could be a key part of  helping them get to the next step  they're gonna want to bring you on board  and if you do a great job and prove  yourself and ask for more work and pour  yourself into this they're going to want  to hire you and you get to choose if you  want to stay at that company or not a  great position to be in believe those  you're watching like the video please  give a thumbs up below it makes you  always want to do more for you and  please leave a comment below let me know  what you think if you have a question  for your company let me know I'll make a  video response thank you so much and  I'll see you soon  you
 

